🚀 Feature

GraphTask::init_to_execute() uses manually unrolled version of depth first search to traverse the autograd graph. The purpose is to determine whether each node/function needs to be computed (calling apply()). A node needs to be computed, iff any of its child nodes needs to be computed.
The method uses an unnecessary any() to check each out edges of a node when all edges are visited. Instead, needed_ of a node can be updated incremental when the following 2 cases happen

Its next edge points to an already visited node, A. A can't be in the stack at the moment, because the graph is a DAG. Therefore, needed_ of A must have finalized. Just update the node's needed_ according to A's.
The node, B, pointed by its next edge just gets popped out of the stack. Then needed_ of B must have been finalized. Just update the node's needed_ according to B's.




